.TH TENGO 1 "2025-05-12" "tengo 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tengo \- fast terminal editor for structured config files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tengo
.RI [ file ...]
.br
.B tengo
.I file
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tengo
is a zero-config terminal text editor optimised for YAML, JSON, TOML, INI,
and XML files.
It can open files interactively or apply transformations non-interactively
from the command line.
.PP
With no flags,
.B tengo
opens the given file(s) in the interactive editor.
With one of the CLI flags below, it applies the operation and exits
immediately \(em no editor is opened.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "CLI mode (non-interactive)"
.TP
.BI \-F " text"
Find all occurrences of
.I text
and print matching lines with line numbers and counts.
.TP
.BI \-R " text"
Replacement text (requires
.BR \-F ).
Prompts for confirmation on each occurrence unless
.B \-\-confirm\-all
is given.
.TP
.B \-\-confirm\-all
Apply all replacements without per-occurrence prompts.
.TP
.B \-\-regex
Treat the
.B \-F
pattern as a regular expression.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show a colored unified diff of what would change without writing to disk.
.TP
.B \-\-stdout
Print the result to stdout instead of saving in place.
.TP
.B \-\-backup
Write a
.I .bak
copy of the original file before any destructive write.
.TP
.B \-validate
Validate file syntax and exit.
Exit code 0 = valid, 1 = invalid, 2 = I/O error.
.TP
.B \-format
Auto-format / pretty-print the file in place.
Supports YAML, JSON, and TOML.
.TP
.BI \-key " path"
Read the value at the dot-notation key path
(e.g.\&
.IR database.host ).
Supports YAML, JSON, and TOML.
.TP
.BI \-set " path" = value
Set the value at the dot-notation key path and save.
Note: the file is re-marshaled, so original formatting and comments are
not preserved.
.TP
.BI \-L " n"
Print line
.I n
(1-based) and exit.
.TP
.BI \-type " ext"
Specify the file type when reading from stdin: yaml, json, toml, xml, ini.
.TP
.B \-q
Suppress output; rely on exit codes only.
.TP
.BI \-completion " shell"
Print a shell completion script for
.I shell
(bash, zsh, or fish) to stdout and exit.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version string and exit.
.TP
.B \-help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH "INTERACTIVE EDITOR SHORTCUTS"
.TS
l l.
Ctrl+S	Save (validates on save)
Ctrl+Q / Esc	Quit
Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y	Undo / Redo
Ctrl+F	Find
Ctrl+R	Find & Replace
Ctrl+E	Validate syntax
Ctrl+T	Format / pretty-print
Ctrl+G	Go to line
Ctrl+N	Toggle line numbers
Alt+W	Toggle word-wrap
Ctrl+A	Select all
Ctrl+C / Ctrl+X / Ctrl+V	Copy / Cut / Paste
Ctrl+] / Ctrl+[	Indent / Outdent
Ctrl+D	Duplicate line
Ctrl+/	Toggle comment
Shift+Enter	Insert line below
Ctrl+Shift+Enter	Insert line above
Ctrl+Left / Ctrl+Right	Word jump + select
Alt+Arrow	Fast navigation (4 steps)
Ctrl+W	Next tab
Alt+1 \(en Alt+9	Switch to tab N
Ctrl+H	Help overlay
.TE
.SH "FILE TYPES"
.TS
l l l l l.
Extension	Highlight	Validate	Format	\-key/\-set
\&.yaml / .yml	yes	yes	yes	yes
\&.json	yes	yes	yes	yes
\&.toml	yes	yes	yes	yes
\&.ini / .cfg	yes	yes	\-	\-
\&.xml	\-	yes	\-	\-
.TE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Open a file in the interactive editor:
.B tengo config.yaml
.TP
Open multiple files in tabs:
.B tengo config.yaml secrets.json
.TP
Validate syntax:
.B tengo config.yaml \-validate
.TP
Find and replace, preview only:
.B tengo config.yaml \-F localhost \-R 0.0.0.0 \-\-dry\-run
.TP
Format in place with a backup:
.B tengo config.json \-format \-\-backup
.TP
Read a key value:
.B tengo config.yaml \-key database.host
.TP
Set a key value:
.B tengo config.yaml \-set database.port=5432
.TP
Validate from stdin:
.B cat config.yaml | tengo \-validate \-type yaml
.TP
Install bash completion:
.B source <(tengo \-completion bash)
.TP
Install zsh completion:
.B tengo \-completion zsh > ~/.zfunc/_tengo
.TP
Install fish completion:
.B tengo \-completion fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/tengo.fish
.SH "EXIT CODES"
.TP
.B 0
Success (or valid when using \-validate).
.TP
.B 1
Invalid syntax, key not found, or no matches.
.TP
.B 2
I/O error or bad arguments.
